Hi Bill,

You might want to check the console "cpu_enabled" variable.  Also check
the console messages while the system is coming up; if the 2nd CPU has
been disabled by the console, the OS will say something like, "CPU x
not started because it's console-disabled."

| cpu_enabled | enables this many CPUs |
+-------------+------------------------+
|      1      |           1            |
+-------------+------------------------+
|      3      |           2            |
+-------------+------------------------+
|      7      |           3            |
+-------------+------------------------+
|      F      |           4            |
+-------------+------------------------+

If you change the value of cpu_enabled, make sure you >>>init the
console right afterwards, otherwise the new value won't "take."
This is a peculiarity of some but not all Alpha platforms.

Hope this helps,

QH


