As per my writings---those which have caused much abuse and angst in the
newsgroups--I believe that T64 is a technically superior solution. While
it's easy for me or any analyst to pontificate and to spend other people's
money, I think the best solution is to rename T64 HP-UX and to leverage the
Intel porting dollars to persuade the HP-UX ISVs to port their apps to HP-UX
Post-Millennium Edition. The result would be a Unix with a modern, modular
kernel.

The HP way will more likely involve grafting the goodness of Tru64 onto the
long-in-tooth HP-UX kernel. This will give Sun, IBM, et al a competitive
knockoff: nice clustering, antiquated kernel.

Just my $0.02




