 true for the OS, but not [neccessarily] true for runtime support. The
OS of course does not know the internals of a binary input file. The RTL
may very well know. The DEC/COMPAQ Frotran compiler has support for
reading/writing binary files both ways. I think it can even convert more
exotic stuff like the old VAX formats. But of course, the RTL "knows"
what to expect when it comes to a binary read.

