> Economical? How valuable is your employers data?

This, like cost-to-acquire vs. TCO, is probably the longest standing
battle for data integrity.

Bean counters only understand the Cash Flow, Balance Sheet, P&L, etc.
They don't understand the value of IP, the contents of the database,
etc. since it tends to be nearly impossible to quantify, and has little
or no impact on the stock price, profits or dividends.

I usually word it these ways:

1. "How much money can you AFFORD to save (or not spend)?"

2. "That's the difference between what *CAN* be done and what *SHOULD*
be done."

A losing battle in both cases. If you can't punch it up on a calculator,
lay it out on a spreadsheet, etc., they ain't list'nin'.

