"setld -i | grep CDE" will tell you what components (if any) of CDE
are installed.  I believe at minimum you need the OSFCDEMINxxx and
OSFCDEDTxxx subsets; on my V5.0 workstation it's named OSFCDEMIN500. 
But I would go ahead and install all the CDE subsets.

Here is the list of subsets installed on my workstation.

OSFCDEAPPS500        installed  CDE Additional Applications (Windows
Applications)
OSFCDEDEV500         installed  CDE Software Development and
Programming Examples(Software Development)
OSFCDEDT500          installed  CDE Desktop Environment (Windowing
Environment)
OSFCDEMAIL500        installed  CDE Mail Interface (Mail Applications)
OSFCDEMANOP500       installed  Ref Pages: CDE Development (Reference
Pages)
OSFCDEMANOS500       installed  Ref Pages: CDE Admin/User (Reference
Pages)
OSFCDEMIN500         installed  CDE Minimum Runtime Environment
(Windowing Environment)
OSFSDECDE500         installed  Software Development Desktop
Environment(Software Development)

Hope this helps,

QH


