reasonable half-height form factor like a DAT drive.  And I believe the
mechanism was being built by a new manufacturer other than Quantum, though 
I can't quite recall the builder's name.  I will say that having a
half-height drive available would dramatically expand the usability of the
format, since there have been several servers over the years that I've not
been able to conveniently put a DLT drive into without going to an external
drive.

