s.smale wrote:
> 
> unclear as to the numbering issues. I am sure in the hsg80 manual it
> states somthing about
> 
> unit number above D100 only being seen by port 2 or something similar. I
> will have another look at the manual at work tomorrow.


That's only with Transparent failover where port D0-D99 is presented via 
port 1 and D100-D199 from port 2 (per HSG).   With Multibus failover 
D0-D199 are presented out of both HSG ports.    

So for full NSPOF you have to cater for the fact that any unit could 
potentially be accessed through any one of 4 ports, and you have to provide 
connectivity to meet that.  BUT, in reality units are assigned to one HSG 
or the other, so I/O will only travel over one pair of ports at a time.  

Combine this with a GS cluster, where to get the most out of the system its 
desirable to give each QBB to its own interface to the SAN to avoid QBB I/O 
travelling over the Heirachical Switch and it presents some interesting 
challenges when designing your SAN. 




