Hello Hannes,

Would it be possible to get more information regarding the disk
layout, how they are connected to the controller(s), Tru64 version and
patch level?  Output of showfdmn and showfsets for the domain under
consideration?

You may be able to get better performance using AdvFS striping (man
stripe).

You may want to move the AdvFS transaction log to a different disk. 
This would be my first suspicion since the transaction log must be
written for all domain fileset activity, and as soon as you move to
the second disk you now need to write to TWO disks (one for data, one
for the transaction log).

Another option would be to use LSM striping assuming you have the
required PAK for that.  I have always had outstanding success with LSM
striping although there is a learning curve associated with it.

Hope this helps in some small measure.

QH


