s.smale wrote:

> 1 I would have thought you would have binned LSM and done all mirroring
> through your cached controllers

You answered that yourself in point (3).  V4.0F does not support 
multi-pathing, so the controllers have to be configured in Transparent 
failover mode and the SAN has to be designed so that there is only one 
connection path between each system and a controller port.

Consequently, if he mirrors on the controller, the mirror will/can only be 
visible to each system via one path (one KGPSA) because the controller pair 
will only present the LUN out of one port at a time (the A or B port of the 
preferred controller).  You said yourself in point (3) that you've had 
KGPSA failures, so this doesn't really qualify to be called High 
Availability any more.

I agree that loosing LSM from the equation at the first opportunity is a 
good idea though.  It adds unwanted and time consuming levels of complexity 
in a disaster recovery situation and isn't needed on V5.1 thanks to the 
introduction of multi-pathing.  That's assuming the disks are laid out in a 
fashon that makes controller mirroring possible.  The current structure of 
the disk farm may not make this easy without a lot of disk juggling.


John



