Your right,

If you connect a keyboard/mouse and monitor to the pci box and then set the
console on your system to graphics.  The problem is that the GS has two
levels of console, SCM and SRM.  In graphics mode the keyboard will not
decode the esc esc scm string that puts you into SCM from SRM.  For
troubleshooting, services needs the console set to serial mode and logging
enabled.

Leave your console set to serial with logging turned on.  If you want, you
can still connect a keyboard/mouse and monitor and have graphics access to
the system.

Regards
