All the potentially installable files are listed in the subset inventory 
files - /usr/.smdb./*.inv - you could sum their contents with 'wc -l' (word 
count).  But if you've got old subsets files from previous upgrades and 
patch kits in there, this would skew things a bit.

Or if you want to know how many files are on your system you could

 # cd /
 # find . -print | wc -l

 



