>I have  a DS20 with True64 4.0G. When booting the system I find the tape at
>mkd400. When coming up to standalone, I want to make the special devices for the
>tape. As I remeber, the formula was BUS-IDx8+SCSI-ID of the device. But this
>failed. During bootup I found a message regarding a tz44, which workes fine.
>
>But: What is the numbering scheme behind this????

Tape devices have two numbers.  One is the internal unit number which
is found from the formula you provide (bus * 8) + scsi-id.  This is
what you use to create the special files using MAKEDEV.  The other
number is the special file number, which is assigned sequentially
starting at zero; rmt0, rmt1, rmt2, etc.

A "tz44" tape would be one on bus 5, target 4.  An MKD400 would be
bus 3 (A = 0, B = 1, C = 2, D = 3) target 4.  It would be "tz28".
The boot messages print the internal unit numbers as it identifies
devices, so that's often the best source to get the name to hand
off to MAKEDEV.

