Hi Derek,

Two things,

Using the rmt0h device driver file should ask the tape drive to write at
max. density.

also, if you look at the drive lights when you put a tape in it, without
anything trying to access it, it reads the calibration tracks of the tape
(whizzes back & forward for a bit) and will then show what density the tape
is set at. If you get the compression light coming on, bob's your auntie, if
not use the density over ride button to select the required density and dump
something (anything) to tape and the calibration tracks will be re-set
accordingly.

Cheers

Dave
