Henry wrote:
> 
> Hi all, I have a Tru64_5.1 box and it is setup NIS the same domain as
> other digital boxes. The problem is if users login the Tru64_5.1 box and
> create a file, it alwasys waits for 30 seconds to let do it (users
> physical account location are on other machines). If user physical
> account is on this Tru64_5.1, there is no delay when create a file even
> users login to other machines.
> 
> Could someone give an advice to stop this delay. I appreciate for any
> suggestion. Thanks.

It doesn't sound like an NIS user problem; I think what is happening is
there is some host IP/name lookup
(DNS or otherwise) failing for the box on the "other machines". If the
problem goes away when the IP
and name of the other machines are in the local /etc/hosts file, then
that's it. Fix the /etc/resolv.conf
(if you're using DNS) so the 1st name server queried can translate back
from IP to names, and you should be OK.

