David Rice wrote:

> How do you set the path for shared libraries. In linux you can just
> edit /etc/ld.so.conf. Is there a similar file for TRU64?

There's no way to set a default search path for the entire system. In each 
process, you can set the environment variable LD_LIBRARY_PATH to a search 
path in which the loader will look for shared libraries. (Setuid binaries, 
though, ignore this, for security.)

