NetBSD works fine on mine, using the framebuffer.  You have to use a
-current snapshot and maybe recompile the kernel, since it defaults
to serial for install.  Other than that, it works fine, and much
faster than the early 4.0D or somesuch DECos that came with it.

Hook a vt100 out the back, install, recompile with tcwscons, and all
should do what you want to do.

AFIK the 1.5W snapshot is what you need /pub/NetBSD/arch/alpha/snapshot.

I booted mine off floppy, since that was available.

It is not a half bad little machine, once you get it going on one of the
big 19 inch monitors....(:+}}...

Bob


